         since the day it shipped: no mailbox has ever been connected. It now leads to
         everything that arrives which she can only look at — the pictures her family posts,
         and letters if a mailbox is ever set up. Named for what she does with all of it,
         because no single noun covers both without lying about half of them. The same rule
